tps://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14129#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. The heads of executive departments and agencies may determine\nthat certain offices and installations of their organizations, or parts thereof,\nmust remain open and that certain employees must report for duty on\nDecember 24, 2024, for reasons of national security, defense, or other public\nneed.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"89 FR 104857 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 2","sha256":"2cdbd85bcaa3453cd5ac38b358dff867202c002b85e53dcb2695d8154fd26254","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14129#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. December 24, 2024, shall be considered as falling within the scope\nof Executive Order 11582 of February 11, 1971, and of 5 U.S.C. 5546 and\n6103(b) and other similar statutes insofar as they relate to the pay and\nleave of employees of the United States.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"89 FR 104857 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3","sha256":"2cdbd85bcaa3453cd5ac38b358dff867202c002b85e53dcb2695d8154fd26254","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14129#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall take\nsuch actions as may be necessary to implement this order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"89 FR 104857 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4","sha256":"2cdbd85bcaa3453cd5ac38b358dff867202c002b85e53dcb2695d8154fd26254","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14129#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Nothing in this order shall be construed\nto impair or otherwise affect:\n(i) the authority granted by law to an executive department or agency,\nor the head thereof; or\n(ii) the functions of the Director of the Office of Management and Budget\nrelating to budgetary, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"89 FR 104857 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"2cdbd85bcaa3453cd5ac38b358dff867202c002b85e53dcb2695d8154fd26254","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14129#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) This order shall be implemented consistent with applicable law and\nsubject to the availability of appropriations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"89 FR 104857 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"2cdbd85bcaa3453cd5ac38b358dff867202c002b85e53dcb2695d8154fd26254","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14129#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit,\nsubstantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity by any party\nagainst the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its officers,\nemployees, or agents, or any other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"89 FR 104858 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 5(c)","sha256":"2cdbd85bcaa3453cd5ac38b358dff867202c002b85e53dcb2695d8154fd26254","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14129#sec5(c)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"whole per-document Federal Register PDF (89 FR 104857)","sha256":"2cdbd85bcaa3453cd5ac38b358dff867202c002b85e53dcb2695d8154fd26254","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-12-26/pdf/2024-31143.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","